      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "LEON RUBEN (4) raced wide but still kept coming to finish fourth last start over 1450m at the Illawarra Grange circuit. Drops 3.5kgs under today's scale and should enjoy the extra trip. Can win a very shallow maiden. WIZARD'S STAR (9) raced handy and whacked away to hang on for a distant third last time out over 2000m at Hawkesbury. Back in trip is not ideal but he is rock hard fit after three runs back and should play a role in the outcome. FLYING ARABESQUE (1) stalked the pace and wasn't beaten all that far last Saturday over 1400m at this track. Sparingly raced four-year-old who steps up to the mile at the right time. MY CARTOUCHE (5) improved sharply last start at Wyong at the third run back from a spell. Big chance if she can hold that form. STAY QUIET (7) disappointed at Newcastle recently but is worth another chance with blinkers on for the first time.",
